# Build output. Each app builds into its own build/; nothing under one is tracked.
build/
*.o
*.a
*.elf
*.prx

# Release staging. Each app's `dist` target writes the artifacts CI publishes into its own
# dist/; it is output, never tracked.
dist/

# A title's origin, fetched at the revision its `upstream.lock` names (src/oops-titles). Fetched
# output, like build/ and dist/ above - ours is the lock, the patches and the shim beside it, and
# committing somebody else's tree would be both a fork and a licence question we do not need to
# have. It also keeps the identity scan's surface to the files we actually wrote.
upstream/

# No `__pycache__/` or `*.pyc` rule, deliberately. There is no Python in this repository and
# there is not meant to be - the build is make and the scripts are shell. An ignore rule for
# bytecode is a quiet accommodation for a language that is not allowed here: it would hide the
# first stray file rather than let `git status` show it.

# Claude Code's per-person overrides. A `settings.json` beside it would be shared; the
# `.local` one is whoever is sitting here.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Whatever the person editing this happens to run.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
